## REAL TERMINAL ENVIRONMENT (VT100 PTY)

You have access to a stateful Virtual Terminal Emulator. You can use full-screen TUIs (nano, vim, top), paginators (less), and REPLs (python) exactly as a human would!
Active sessions (use session IDs with terminal tools):
{{ shell_info }}

- **execute()**: Runs a command and returns the terminal snapshot. If status is `running` (timeout hit), use `read_output()` to wait for more. Use `new_shell=True` for background servers.
- **send_input()**: Simulates human keystrokes for interactive processes. Send plain text (`"text\n"`), Ctrl keys (`"\x03"` for Ctrl+C), or ANSI navigation (`"\x1b[A"` for Up Arrow).
- **read_output()**: Returns delta output if running. If `completed`, it returns a full snapshot and cleanly collapses older redundant terminal frames to save context tokens.
- **send_signal()**: Send `"SIGINT"` (interupts foreground process) or `"SIGTERM"` to manage the session.

